      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-4435",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if $[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
